    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</em></p><p>This small sphere of thick glass weighs 1 pound. While you are within 60 feet of it, you can command it to shed light like that of the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplLight00000]{Light} or the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDaylight00]{Daylight} spell (your choice). Once the Daylight effect has been used, it can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p><p>As a Magic action, you can give another command to make the glowing globe rise into the air and float no more than 5 feet off the ground. It hovers like this until you or another creature grabs it. If you move more than 60 feet away from the hovering globe, it follows you by the shortest route until it is within 60 feet of you. If something stops it from moving, the globe sinks gently to the ground, becomes inactive, and its light goes out.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-P0hwewylBJ94vaID\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p><em>Light</em> et <em>Daylight</em> appliquent la lumière (1 heure) au jeton de celui qui commande le globe : retirez-la si le globe s’éloigne ou s’éteint.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
